    "review": "The hero died while starving under prison guard pressure. Decision 2964's accepted transition records HP 5 to 0; it does not establish the killer. Earlier, entrance-shop search exhaustion caused 201 advancing-time fallback waits on floor six. A separate, directly evidenced defect initiated repeated full-pack loot loops: decisions 2794–2798 repeatedly clicked the persistent pasty without advancing time, and decision 2799 reported a navigation loop. For the upgrade pickup, decision 2828 explicitly reports the occupied floor blocked by prior movement bookkeeping after full-pack refusal. The selecting chain confuses pickup refusal with failed movement. The proposed focused correction retains floor reachability and defers ordinary collection until inventory changes only when an existing public full-pack receipt matches; mandatory resources remain outstanding. A new reduced regression fails on the played policy and passes on the candidate. All 1410 Python tests pass, with four skipped. This does not prove pack relief or survival, and unidentified potions are not counted as known healing. Policy and regression changes are local proposals; files is empty because the trusted adapter derives them.",
    "learnings": "A verified underfoot pickup refusal is not evidence that occupied ground is impassable. Preserve honest loot obligations and hazard checks; reopen ordinary collection after inventory changes without granting acquisition or descent credit."
